#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""heronctl: one way to look at, deploy to and test every Heron computer.

  heronctl status                     every computer at a glance (read-only)
  heronctl diff                       which installed files differ from this checkout
  heronctl deploy [--dry-run]         install this checkout's Heron files, restart the keepers
  heronctl logs [-f] [-n N]           keeper logs of every computer, prefixed
  heronctl wait REGEX… [--timeout S]  until keeper log lines match every regex (instead of sleep + tail)
  heronctl tasks [--all]              the background-task board
  heronctl task start TITLE BRIEF     put a dev task on the board (no chat, no report to anyone)
  heronctl task show|stop|rm ID       its state, log and result; stop it; remove it (dev tasks only)
  heronctl chat where                 which computer runs the Heron chat
  heronctl chat read [-n N] [--live]  the last messages
  heronctl chat send TEXT [--wait S] [--live] [--on HOST]
                                      message the dev chat ("Heron dev"); --live: the real one
  heronctl chat cleanup               archive the dev chat
  heronctl kill HOST [--hard]         take a computer's Zeron down (--hard: keeper, sync, task runs too)
  heronctl revive [HOST…]             bring back what `kill` took down (default: everything killed)
  heronctl test-mode on|off|status    short failover timings on every computer, and back

Every command takes --hosts air,zeph,mbp to narrow it. Computers and how to
reach them: HOSTS below, overridden per computer by ~/.heron/hosts.json
(a list of {"name", "ssh", ...}). The computer you are on is used directly.
A computer is reached by its ssh alias when this computer's ~/.ssh/config has
one, else as user@ its Tailscale name, so no ssh config is needed.

Remote work is a Python script piped to `ssh HOST python3 -`, so nothing is
ever quoted for a remote shell (the MacBook's login shell is fish).
Standard library only; runs on macOS's /usr/bin/python3 (3.9).
"""
